    {
      "message": {
        "content": "{\n  \"chapter_id\": \"CH02\",\n  \"chapter_argument\": \"肠道微生物群通过特定的分类学特征与代谢物谱系统性调节实体瘤 ICI 疗效，但现有证据呈现高度的情境依赖性（癌种、治疗方案、宿主背景）。观察性关联已确立特定菌群与代谢物的预后价值，而定量代谢组学与菌株分辨率研究正推动生物标志物从“物种丰度”向“功能通路”演进；然而，人类肿瘤微环境内代谢物绝对浓度的缺失及跨队列泛化能力的不足，限制了其作为独立临床决策工具的转化就绪度。\",\n  \"units\": [\n    {\n      \"unit_id\": \"CH02_U01\",\n      \"focus\": \"特定菌属/种的富集与 ICI 响应相关，但效应方向高度依赖癌种与治疗策略，单一通用标志物难以成立。\",\n      \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"CH02_U01_P01\",\n          \"point\": \"跨癌种反复出现的阳性与阴性标志物（如 Faecalibacterium, Bacteroidales）存在，但其预测效力受治疗方案（联合 vs. 单药）显著修饰。\",\n          \"development\": \"先综述跨癌种的通用关联趋势，随后引入治疗背景（CICB vs. 抗 PD-1 单药，NIC vs. PC）对菌群效应方向的修饰作用，最后指出不同研究间结果不一致的根源在于治疗背景与人群异质性，呼应表格中的对比数据。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0592\",\n              \"role\": \"背景\",\n              \"use\": \"提供跨癌种常见阳性（Faecalibacterium 等）与阴性（Bacteroidales 等）标志物的定性综合。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0598\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供菌株水平特征仅适用于 CICB 方案而在单药队列中预测力降至随机水平的关键证据。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0567\",\n              \"role\": \"例证\",\n              \"use\": \"展示 NSCLC 中特定菌属（Fusicatenibacter 等）与 OS 的关联在 NIC 臂显著而在 PC 臂较弱的实例。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"table_tasks\": [\n        {\n          \"table_id\": \"CH02_U01_T01\",\n          \"purpose\": \"比较不同研究背景下微生物特征与 ICI 疗效关联的异质性，突显治疗方案的修饰作用。\",\n          \"columns\": [\n            \"研究来源\",\n            \"癌种与治疗背景\",\n            \"关键微生物特征\",\n            \"关联方向与预测性能\"\n          ],\n          \"row_tasks\": [\n            {\n              \"content\": \"P0598：黑色素瘤及外部队列，比较 CICB 与抗 PD-1 单药方案下的菌株特征预测力。\",\n              \"source_uses\": [\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0598\",\n                  \"role\": \"比较\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供 CICB 方案下 AUC 0.85 与单药方案下预测力降至随机水平的具体数据。\"\n                }\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"content\": \"P0567：NSCLC 新辅助治疗，比较 NIC（免疫联合）与 PC（化疗）臂下的菌群 - 生存期关联。\",\n              \"source_uses\": [\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0567\",\n                  \"role\": \"比较\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供 Fusicatenibacter 等菌属在 NIC 臂显著关联 OS 而在 PC 臂较弱的对比数据。\"\n                }\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"content\": \"P0592：多癌种综述，汇总不同实体瘤中常见菌属的预后关联趋势。\",\n              \"source_uses\": [\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0592\",\n                  \"role\": \"比较\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供 Faecalibacterium 等菌属在多种实体瘤中普遍关联良好预后的定性总结。\"\n                }\n              ]\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"unit_id\": \"CH02_U02\",\n      \"focus\": \"粪便与血浆中的 SCFAs 及肌苷浓度提供定量预后信号，但缺乏肿瘤组织内绝对浓度数据，限制机制外推与因果推断。\",\n      \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"CH02_U02_P01\",\n          \"point\": \"系统循环与粪便代谢物（SCFAs、肌苷）的具体浓度值与生存期存在统计关联，但肿瘤间质液数据的缺失阻碍了局部机制的确证。\",\n          \"development\": \"首先报告粪便/血浆中 SCFAs（丙酸、丁酸等）的具体浓度值及其与 PFS/OS 的统计关联，随后引入肌苷的机制潜力，最后明确指出人类肿瘤组织中代谢物空间重分布与定量浓度数据的缺失，阐明为何局部浓度缺失限制了因果推断。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0092\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供响应者与非响应者粪便丙酸中位浓度（172.6 vs 103.6 μmol/g）及多变量 Cox 模型 HR 值。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0595\",\n              \"role\": \"例证\",\n              \"use\": \"提供 NSCLC 患者中长期响应者粪便多种 SCFA 及烟酸水平显著高于早期进展者的代谢组学证据。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0590\",\n              \"role\": \"局限\",\n              \"use\": \"指出肌苷增强 ICI 疗效的机制（UBA6 抑制）及人类肿瘤组织中肌苷定量浓度数据目前缺失的现状。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"unit_id\": \"CH02_U03\",\n      \"focus\": \"菌株水平宏基因组分析揭示种内功能异质性，功能通路预测效力优于单一物种丰度，但实验性功能验证仍待完成。\",\n      \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"CH02_U03_P01\",\n          \"point\": \"菌株分辨率与功能通路（如丁酸生成）显著提升预测 AUC，但内源性关联菌株的实验性因果验证尚缺。\",\n          \"development\": \"展示菌株参考库如何提升机器学习预测性能，列举关键功能基因簇（乙酰辅酶 A 丁酸生成途径）与表型的逻辑链条，随后引入益生菌干预的菌株特异性案例，最后指出当前研究多依赖基因组注释，需结合实验验证实际功能。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0598\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供菌株水平丰度预测 AUC（0.85）优于物种水平（0.67）及正向关联菌株拥有完整丁酸生成途径的证据。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0597\",\n              \"role\": \"例证\",\n              \"use\": \"提供特定益生菌（CBM588）在 mRCC 中提升 PFS 的案例，强调菌株特异性效应及缺乏内源性菌株因果验证。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0592\",\n              \"role\": \"发展\",\n              \"use\": \"强调功能通路（SCFA 合成等）比分类学组成更能稳定预测 ICI 结局，指出需结合宏转录组确认实际代谢通量。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"unit_id\": \"CH02_U04\",\n      \"focus\": \"现有证据支持微生物组作为 ICI 疗效的预测维度，但转化就绪度受限于方法学异质性、因果链条未闭合及缺乏大型 III 期验证。\",\n      \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"CH02_U04_P01\",\n          \"point\": \"微生物特征具备预测潜力，但标准化缺失、跨队列泛化能力不足及缺乏 III 期 RCT 限制了其作为独立临床决策工具。\",\n          \"development\": \"综合前述证据层级，指出当前共识（抗生素管理可建议，但 FMT/代谢物干预需等待验证），强调跨队列验证中模型性能的波动，最后总结技术标准化、多中心前瞻性队列及代谢物空间定量是跨越“相关性”至“功能性”的关键步骤。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0592\",\n              \"role\": \"背景\",\n              \"use\": \"总结缺乏统一生物标志物签名及 FMT 需大规模 RCT 确证的现状。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0598\",\n              \"role\": \"局限\",\n              \"use\": \"提供跨队列验证中模型预测性能波动（AUC 0.60–0.65）及需克服批次效应的证据。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0582\",\n              \"role\": \"发展\",\n              \"use\": \"强调临床转化面临技术标准化缺失、个体基线差异大及监管路径不明确等挑战，建议优先实施抗生素管理。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}",
        "reasoning_content": "The user wants me to act as a **Chapter Editor** for a review article chapter (CH02).\nMy task is to organize the writing tasks for this chapter based on the provided input data.\nI need to:\n1.  **Allocate all selected sources** (`sources`) to paragraph tasks or table tasks.\n2.  **Organize sources with only case uses** (`current_uses` where `kind=case`) into paragraphs or tables.\n3.  **Define paragraph tasks**: `point`, `development`, and `source_uses` (role & use).\n4.  **Reference existing paragraph tasks** if any (currently `existing_paragraph_tasks` is empty in the input, so I will create new ones using the format `<unit_id>_P<01>`).\n5.  **Create tables** only if there is genuine comparative value.\n6.  **Ensure every source handle** from the input `sources` list appears in either `source_uses` or `unused_sources`.\n7.  **Output a specific JSON structure**.\n\n**Input Analysis:**\n- **Chapter ID**: CH02\n- **Units**: 4 units (CH02_U01 to CH02_U04).\n- **Sources**: P0092, P0567, P0582, P0590, P0592, P0595, P0597, P0598. (Total 8 sources).\n- **Existing Paragraph Tasks**: Empty list `[]`. I need to create new paragraph IDs.\n- **Case Level Uses**: Provided for each unit, mapping sources to units.\n- **Open Questions**: Note gaps in data (e.g., lack of intratumoral metabolite concentrations).\n\n**Plan:**\n1.  **Unit 1 (Taxonomic Features)**:\n    -   Focus: Specific genera/species enrichment correlates with ICI response, but context-dependent.\n    -   Sources: P0598 (strain vs species, CICB vs mono), P0567 (NSCLC, specific taxa), P0592 (Review summary of taxa).\n    -   Structure: One or two paragraphs.\n    -   P0598: Main evidence for strain-level superiority and treatment context.\n    -   P0567: Example of treatment context (NIC vs PC).\n    -   P0592: Background/Summary of common taxa.\n\n2.  **Unit 2 (Metabolites)**:\n    -   Focus: SCFAs & Inosine provide quantitative signals, but lack tumor tissue data.\n    -   Sources: P0092 (SCFA concentrations in feces/plasma), P0595 (Metabolomics in NSCLC), P0590 (Inosine mechanism & gap).\n    -   Structure: One paragraph for SCFAs (quantitative data), one for Inosine (mechanism + gap). Or combine if flow allows. Let's make one strong paragraph on quantitative evidence and limitations.\n    -   P0092: Quantitative SCFA data (fecal).\n    -   P0595: Metabolomics profiling (NSCLC).\n    -   P0590: Inosine mechanism + explicit statement on missing tumor tissue data.\n\n3.  **Unit 3 (Strain/Function)**:\n    -   Focus: Strain-level analysis reveals functional heterogeneity; pathway > species.\n    -   Sources: P0598 (Strain library, pathways), P0597 (Probiotic intervention example), P0592 (Functional pathways review).\n    -   Structure: One paragraph on strain/function superiority.\n    -   P0598: Strain library & pathway evidence (butyrate).\n    -   P0597: Intervention example (probiotics) showing strain specificity.\n    -   P0592: Review support for functional pathways over taxonomy.\n\n4.  **Unit 4 (Translation/Limitations)**:\n    -   Focus: Evidence supports prediction but translation limited by heterogeneity, lack of causality, no Phase III.\n    -   Sources: P0592 (Lack of unified signature, FMT needs RCT), P0598 (Cross-cohort validation波动), P0582 (Translation challenges, stewardship).\n    -   Structure: One paragraph summarizing readiness.\n    -   P0592: General limitation summary.\n    -   P0598: Validation performance drop.\n    -   P0582: Translation framework & challenges.\n\n**Check Source Allocation:**\n- P0092 -> U02\n- P0567 -> U01\n- P0582 -> U04\n- P0590 -> U02\n- P0592 -> U01, U03, U04 (Can be used multiple times for different points)\n- P0595 -> U02\n- P0597 -> U03\n- P0598 -> U01, U03, U04\n\n**Table Consideration:**\n- Unit 1 could have a table comparing taxa across cancer types/treatments, but the sources are reviews or specific studies. P0592 is a review summarizing taxa. P0567 and P0598 are specific studies. A table might be useful to show \"Taxa - Cancer - Treatment - Effect\".\n- However, the instruction says \"Only make a table if there is genuine comparative value\". Given the heterogeneity emphasized in the thesis (\"context-dependent\"), a table summarizing the *inconsistency* might be good. But P0592 is a review summarizing many. P0567 and P0598 are specific.\n- Let's stick to paragraphs for now to ensure flow, unless the comparison is sharp. The prompt asks to organize sources into paragraphs or tables. I will prioritize paragraphs as the primary narrative flow, but I can add a table in Unit 1 if it helps compare the \"Context Dependency\".\n- Actually, Unit 1's point is \"effect direction highly depends on cancer type & treatment\". A table comparing P0598 (CICB vs Mono) and P0567 (NIC vs PC) and P0592 (General summary) could illustrate this well.\n- Let's create a table for Unit 1 to visualize the context dependency.\n- Columns: Study/Source, Context (Cancer/Treatment), Key Taxa/Feature, Outcome/Association.\n- Rows: P0598, P0567, P0592 (as summary).\n\n**Refining Paragraph Tasks:**\n- I need to ensure `existing_paragraph_tasks` are referenced. The input says `existing_paragraph_tasks`: [] (empty). So I will create new IDs like `CH02_U01_P01`.\n- I must ensure every source is used.\n- P0592 is used in U01, U03, U04. This is allowed (\"Same paper can be used in different paragraphs, but purpose must be different\").\n- P0598 is used in U01, U03, U04.\n- I need to make sure the `source_uses` in the JSON reflect the specific role in *that* paragraph.\n\n**Drafting the JSON:**\n- **Chapter Argument**: Summarize the chapter's thesis (Taxonomy -> Metabolites -> Strains/Function -> Translation Limits).\n- **Units**:\n    - U01: Taxonomy & Context. Table for comparison. Paragraph for synthesis.\n    - U02: Metabolites (SCFA/Inosine) & Data Gaps.\n    - U03: Strain/Function Resolution.\n    - U04: Translation & Limitations.\n\n**Wait, one constraint:** \"Reference existing paragraph tasks... Each existing paragraph id must be referenced by at least one task.\"\n- Input `existing_paragraph_tasks` is `[]`. So I don't need to reference any existing IDs. I will create new ones.\n\n**Constraint Check:** \"Every source handle in input `sources` must appear in some paragraph's `source_uses` or some table row's `source_uses` or `unused_sources`.\"\n- Sources: P0092, P0567, P0582, P0590, P0592, P0595, P0597, P0598.\n- I will distribute them.\n\n**Table Design for U01:**\n- Purpose: Compare how taxonomic associations vary by treatment context.\n- Rows: P0598 (CICB vs Mono), P0567 (NIC vs PC), P0592 (General Review).\n- This highlights the \"Context Dependency\" thesis.\n\n**Paragraph Design:**\n- U01 P01: Narrative synthesis of the table (General taxa + Context dependency).\n- U02 P01: SCFA quantitative evidence (P0092, P0595) + Inosine mechanism/gap (P0590).\n- U03 P01: Strain-level advantage & Functional pathways (P0598, P0597, P0592).\n- U04 P01: Translation readiness & Limitations (P0592, P0598, P0582).\n\n**Double Check Source Usage:**\n- P0092: U02 P01\n- P0567: U01 Table & P01\n- P0582: U04 P01\n- P0590: U02 P01\n- P0592: U01 Table & P01, U03 P01, U04 P01 (Multiple uses OK)\n- P0595: U02 P01\n- P0597: U03 P01\n- P0598: U01 Table & P01, U03 P01, U04 P01 (Multiple uses OK)\n\n**Wait, I need to be careful with `source_uses` in Table vs Paragraph.**\n- If a source is in a Table Row, it counts as used.\n- If a source is in a Paragraph, it counts as used.\n- I can list them in both if they support both.\n- To keep it clean, I will put the specific comparative data in the Table, and the narrative synthesis in the Paragraph.\n- Actually, the instruction says: \"Organize sources with only case uses into paragraphs or tables\".\n- I will ensure every source is listed in at least one `source_uses` array (either paragraph or table row).\n\n**Let's finalize the structure.**\n- **U01**:\n    - Table: `CH02_U01_T01`. Rows for P0598, P0567, P0592.\n    - Paragraph: `CH02_U01_P01`. Synthesis of the table + general statement. Sources: P0598, P0567, P0592.\n- **U02**:\n    - Paragraph: `CH02_U02_P01`. SCFA data (P0092, P0595) + Inosine gap (P0590).\n- **U03**:\n    - Paragraph: `CH02_U03_P01`. Strain/Function (P0598, P0597, P0592).\n- **U04**:\n    - Paragraph: `CH02_U04_P01`. Translation (P0592, P0598, P0582).\n\n**Wait, P0592 and P0598 are used in multiple units.**\n- In U01: Focus on Taxa/Context.\n- In U03: Focus on Strain/Function.\n- In U04: Focus on Limitations/Validation.\n- This is allowed (\"Same paper can be used in different paragraphs, but purpose must be different\").\n\n**One detail:** \"Reference existing paragraph tasks...\". Since `existing_paragraph_tasks` is empty, I ignore this constraint regarding *existing* IDs, but I must create new IDs.\n\n**One more detail:** \"Open Questions\". I should not write them as solved. I will ensure the text tasks reflect the gaps (e.g., P0590 explicitly mentions missing tumor tissue data).\n\n**JSON Structure Validation:**\n- `chapter_id`: \"CH02\"\n- `chapter_argument`: 2-4 sentences.\n- `units`: Array of 4 units.\n- `paragraph_tasks`: Array within each unit.\n- `table_tasks`: Array within each unit (optional).\n- `unused_sources`: Array (optional, hopefully empty).\n\n**Self-Correction on Table:**\n- The instruction says: \"Only make a table if there is genuine comparative value\".\n- U01 compares how associations change by treatment (CICB vs Mono, NIC vs PC). This is genuine comparative value showing heterogeneity.\n- I will include the table.\n\n**Source Handle Check:**\n- P0092: U02\n- P0567: U01\n- P0582: U04\n- P0590: U02\n- P0592: U01, U03, U04\n- P0595: U02\n- P0597: U03\n- P0598: U01, U03, U04\n- All 8 sources accounted for.\n\n**Writing the `point` and `development`:**\n- Must be actionable for the writer.\n- `point`: The judgment the reader should get.\n- `development`: Logic flow (e.g., \"Start with X, then contrast with Y\").\n\n**Let's construct the JS